<title>UK: UK govt. says Rosyth sale talks making progress.</title>
<headline>UK govt. says Rosyth sale talks making progress.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Defence said on Wednesday that talks on the sale of the Rosyth naval base in Scotland to a consortium of local businesses &quot;are making good progress.&quot;</p>
<p>In a joint statement, the UK ministry and the consortium, Rosyth 2000 Ltd, said they hope to achieve a handover of the base later this year.</p>
<p>The consortium plans to develop the naval base to include industrial, commercial, leisure and residential uses.</p>
<p>Adjacent dockyards are being sold off separately.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
